WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.602
We have breaking news just in to CNN.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.103
The House

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.304
Homeland Security Committee

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.939
will formally begin impeachment

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:06.773
proceedings

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:09.776
against DHS Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.277
CNN's Lauren Fox joins us

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.912
now from Washington, D.C..

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.615
And Laura, what details do you have?

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.617
Yeah, we are learning more information

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.651
that in this new year,

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.753
the House Republicans

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.621
are planning to forge ahead

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.822
with an impeachment

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.391
against Alejandro Mayorkas,

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.092
the secretary of homeland Security.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.327
Obviously, this comes

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.795
at a really complicated

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.297
political moment for House Republicans

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.500
and for the Congress at large.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.301
That is because right now

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.037
there is bipartisan efforts

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:37.837
in the United States

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.105
Senate to try to reach

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.174
some kind of framework agreement

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.776
that could actually improve

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:44.878
border security along the U.S.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:45.979
southern border.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.547
Those talks have been hard fought.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.115
They've been going on for weeks.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:49.983
And while they don't

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:50.884
have an agreement yet,

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.552
they are trying to reach one

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.287
in order to pass this larger

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.321
supplemental package,

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.022
which would include

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.357
funding for Ukraine

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.859
and Israel as well as money for the U.S.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:00.960
southern border.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.362
But this dynamic

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.130
now that the House Republicans

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:04.531
are planning

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.132
to move forward with this impeachment

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.401
proceedings against New York is shows

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.703
you just how hard it is going to be,

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.173
even if the Senate can reach a deal

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.040
to get that deal

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.076
through the House of Representatives.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.610
So right now, there's a

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.646
this is a complicating dynamic

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.480
as the Senate

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.315
is continuing those efforts.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:23.416
And they're in Washington

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.284
working today

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.385
to try to find

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.086
an agreement

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.353
on that bipartisan border

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.122
security proposal.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:31.658
All right, Lauren, thanks so much.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:32.959
And joining us now is Homeland

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.561
Security Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.629
Mr. Secretary, appreciate your time.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.897
This was not planned.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:38.431
This way,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.566
but since

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.433
the House Republicans

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.468
have telegraphed for a while

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:42.302
that they wanted to move

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.337
in this direction or plan to now

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.238
appear to be doing so,

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.539
I think what my colleague

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.373
Laura was just talking about

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.808
is the critical point here.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.844
You are so deeply engaged

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:51.945
in the border negotiations

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.480
that are going on in the Senate.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.981
Does this undercut

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:55.849
any possibility

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:59.953
of getting a deal under the House floor?

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.454
Oh, I certainly hope not.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.056
Phil, and thanks very much

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.657
for having me this morning.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.092
You know, yesterday

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.495
I joined the bipartisan group of senators

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:10.830
who are negotiating

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:15.235
a solution to a much

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.170
plagued

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.039
broken immigration system.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:20.907
I was very privileged

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:24.344
to participate in that before I did so.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:27.046
I was hard at work in the office

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.381
with my colleagues

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.550
addressing the situation at the border

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.819
and addressing the many other challenges

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:33.486
that the Department

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.321
of Homeland Security confronts.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.157
And after I participated

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.658
in those negotiations

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.059
in providing technical

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.828
and operational advice

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.830
to the bipartisan group of Senators,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.598
I returned to the office

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.266
to perform

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.267
the work of the Department

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.735
of Homeland Security.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.904
We have a broken immigration system.

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:53.173
That is the one single fact about which

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.908
everyone agrees,

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.442
and our administration

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.144
is focused on solutions.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.013
And we're really pleased to join

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:01.881
a bipartisan group of senators

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.884
who are similarly focused on solutions.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.852
Is there.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.753
And I think one of the questions

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.520
that I've had over the course

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.254
the last two weeks,

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.757
and I don't think I'm alone in this, is

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.292
even if you guys reach a deal

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.393
or if the senators reach a deal

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:14.093
and you've obviously been

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.529
providing the technical assistance

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.463
at length over the course

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:18.631
of the last couple of weeks,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.666
is there any commitment

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.099
that House

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.501
Republicans will move

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.969
forward on an agreement

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.103
if they get 60 senators,

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.104
especially when

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:25.939
not only is there impeachment,

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:26.606
but the speaker

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.974
and I think dozens of his colleagues

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.609
will be at the border

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:33.580
today talking about this issue.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:34.948
Well,

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:35.982
when they're at the border,

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.951
they're going to see the magnitude

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:38.851
of the problem

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.920
and why we have said now

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.622
for about three decades

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:43.890
that our broken

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.959
immigration system is in desperate

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.794
need of legislative reform.

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:50.163
So we are focused on solutions,

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.798
and we hope that they will return

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:52.832
to Washington

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.401
and focus on the solutions as well.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.403
Are you communicating with House

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.171
Republican leadership,

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:01.641
with the speaker's office right now?

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:02.508
Right now,

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.510
I am focused on providing the technical

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.212
and operational advice

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.513
that is

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.249
that the bipartisan group of senators

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.817
have asked me to provide

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:13.253
and I feel very privileged to do so.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.687
You're not only

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:17.090
are we doing that to advance

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.091
the negotiations,

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.592
we're very focused on them.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.893
But we've also submitted

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:21.794
this administration

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:22.729
has submitted

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:24.464
a package to Congress

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.199
for additional resources

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:27.800
to plus up the number of Border

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.935
Patrol agents

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:31.504
to plus up the number of asylum officers,

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.507
immigration judges to infuse

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:37.810
our system with much needed resources.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:38.745
You know, to that point,

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.680
we talk a lot about what happens

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.548
if the Ukraine aid runs out.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:43.583
Are you at risk?

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.285
Is DHS at risk

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.619
without this national security

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:47.687
supplemental package

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:48.955
of running out of funding?

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.790
And what happens in that case,

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.592
given how stretched

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.092
the border

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:53.826
and the government

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:56.963
is at the border right now?

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.966
We will not have the resources

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:00.900
to perform

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.070
our jobs as fully and completely

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.605
as we could do so.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.572
And that would be

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.341
a very sad state of affairs.

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:09.309
When do you have a date

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:12.278
on those additional resources?

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.346
We need them now.

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.515
And that is why the president

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:18.518
submitted a supplemental funding package

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.153
quite some time ago.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.488
We need additional personnel

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.991
to advance our security at the border.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.626
We need to acknowledge

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:29.562
to advance our fight against fentanyl.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:32.131
We need additional asylum officers

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.433
to really accelerate

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:35.568
the asylum adjudication process

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.203
so people are not waiting

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.037
six years

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:40.206
before they receive their results,

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:43.209
which is, in effect, a key factor.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:45.111
The fact that people can stay here

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.612
for six years

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:49.082
before their asylum cases adjudicated.

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.516
Is a powerful example

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.150
of how broken

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.152
our immigration system is

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:55.355
and has been for so long.

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:57.757
We have a backlog of cases

00:05:57.757 --> 00:05:59.759
of about 3 million

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.961
in immigration court proceedings

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:03.529
that has been building year

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:06.032
over year over year for decades.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.066
Now,

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:07.600
when it comes,

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.835
I want to get to the specifics

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:09.635
of what you're talking

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.536
with the border crisis

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:11.037
and the issues

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:11.904
you guys have been dealing with

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:14.006
or stretched to try and deal with.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:15.241
But what

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:16.843
I am interested,

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:18.511
have you closed out any issues

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:20.413
in the bipartisan negotiations,

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:22.248
the discussions that have been ongoing?

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:23.916
And do you feel like the issues

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:24.817
that we've been talking about

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:25.284
over the course

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.153
of the last couple of months

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.020
raising credible fear

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.155
standard for asylum seekers

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.390
expelling migrants at the border?

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.592
Would that have a tangible reduction

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:35.695
in border crossings?

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.330
So, Phil, I'm not going to

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.398
get into the particulars

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:39.365
of the negotiations.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.967
I will say this,

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:43.069
that the negotiations have made

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:44.570
the negotiators have made

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.472
substantial progress.

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:48.841
They are focused on solutions

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.576
and they are focused on solutions

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:53.446
that will that will deliver results.

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:56.449
And improve a broken system,

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:58.484
including and very importantly,

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.520
a broken asylum system.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.255
When we talk about numbers,

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:03.256
ABC News is reporting

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:04.223
there are over 300,000

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.425
border encounters in December.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:06.259
CNN has reported

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:08.194
or 225,000 were apprehensions

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:09.429
from illegal crossings.

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:10.596
These are record numbers.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:11.864
This has been a continuous

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:13.566
trend line right now.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.368
Is there anything on the executive

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.636
authority side

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:17.570
that you haven't done yet

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:18.471
that you think you can

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:21.474
that can stem this?

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:22.742
We are focused

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:25.411
on the fundamental solution

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.480
to a long, existing problem.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.582
And that fundamental solution

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:31.017
is legislation.

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:33.286
We have taken actions already

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:35.054
to build lawful pathways

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:36.856
to deliver consequences

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:38.124
and do what we can.

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:40.092
We've promulgated regulations

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:41.527
to do what we can

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:43.062
within the confines of the law.

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:44.797
But fundamentally,

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:46.232
the law is the laws

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:48.234
themselves must change.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:49.268
And this is something

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.437
about which everyone, one agrees,

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:52.705
and that is quite rare

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.740
when one is speaking about immigration.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:55.741
Yeah, it's not the only thing

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:56.375
and immigration

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:57.977
that anybody seems to agree

00:07:57.977 --> 00:07:59.612
with on some level.

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:00.246
Sir, can I ask you

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:01.747
just on a personal level,

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:02.782
you've been in this job

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:04.984
since the start of the administration.

00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:06.419
I think you take heat on a lot of issues.

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:07.854
You have a massive agency

00:08:07.854 --> 00:08:09.222
that draws heat on

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:11.924
just about everything that you guys do.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:12.592
The idea

00:08:12.592 --> 00:08:16.362
of of impeachment proceedings starting.

00:08:16.462 --> 00:08:18.164
Does that affect you at all in a personal

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:18.731
I know you work

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:19.765
and you continue to do the work,

00:08:19.765 --> 00:08:24.103
but what do you think when you see that,

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.338
you know, feel?

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:30.710
I come to the office every morning and

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.813
I am surrounded by incredible,

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:36.749
talented and dedicated people

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:39.719
and it is extraordinarily motivating

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:40.553
to see the work

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:41.587
they do

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:44.590
to witness firsthand their selflessness,

00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:47.860
their talent, their tireless dedication.

00:08:47.927 --> 00:08:50.763
Many sacrifice a tremendous amount.

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:52.231
That's what I think about.

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:53.366
And I'm incredibly proud

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:54.634
to work alongside them

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:56.068
and to support them

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:57.103
in advancing the mission

00:08:57.103 --> 00:08:58.738
of the Department of Homeland Security

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:00.640
on behalf of the American people

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.742
under President Biden's leadership.

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:04.810
That's what I think about every day.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.479
And I'm incredibly proud

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:09.482
of coming to work every day and leaving

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:13.319
the office as late as it might be.

00:09:13.386 --> 00:09:13.786
Having

00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:14.854
done the work with

00:09:14.854 --> 00:09:16.889
such extraordinary people.

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:17.823
Last one before I let you go.

00:09:17.823 --> 00:09:18.824
You've been engaged

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:19.892
in bilateral discussions

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:21.661
with your counterparts in Mexico.

00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:22.929
Pretty critical discussions

00:09:22.929 --> 00:09:24.830
with Mexican officials are going to come

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:25.865
to the United States soon.

00:09:25.865 --> 00:09:27.366
Have you seen a tangible effect

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:28.701
of what you guys

00:09:28.701 --> 00:09:29.735
have discussed up to this point,

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:30.002
what you've

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:33.673
started to implement up to this point?

00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:35.942
So, Phil, we we've started to see

00:09:35.942 --> 00:09:36.542
some results.

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:39.512
These are not results that occur.

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:41.814
The the flick of a switch.

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:43.382
I also have an engagement

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:45.851
with my counterpart from Panama later

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:46.819
this week.

00:09:46.819 --> 00:09:49.822
The issue of migration is a regional one.

00:09:49.922 --> 00:09:51.657
The challenge is a regional one

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:53.359
and requires regional solutions,

00:09:53.359 --> 00:09:55.528
which is why Secretary Blinken,

00:09:55.528 --> 00:09:56.329
Homeland Security

00:09:56.329 --> 00:09:57.697
Adviser SHERWOOD-RANDALL

00:09:57.697 --> 00:09:58.364
and I

00:09:58.364 --> 00:09:59.899
and our entire delegation

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:01.734
was down in Mexico last week.

00:10:01.734 --> 00:10:04.737
And why I will be traveling there again

00:10:04.971 --> 00:10:07.540
and will be traveling in other parts

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:08.674
of the hemisphere

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:09.675
to address

00:10:09.675 --> 00:10:11.010
a regional solution

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.279
to what is a regional challenge.

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:15.047
At the same time,

00:10:15.047 --> 00:10:16.248
with respect to the interest

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:17.683
of the United States

00:10:17.683 --> 00:10:19.251
and our southern border,

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:20.920
most particularly,

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:22.922
it is Congress that must act.

00:10:22.922 --> 00:10:24.323
And I am hopeful

00:10:24.323 --> 00:10:26.258
that the bipartisan group of senators

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:28.861
will achieve a legislative solution,

00:10:28.861 --> 00:10:30.796
that the entire Congress will pass

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:31.864
and we will

00:10:31.864 --> 00:10:33.499
we will see reform

00:10:33.499 --> 00:10:35.234
that has long been needed.

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:36.535
Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas,

00:10:36.535 --> 00:10:39.939
we appreciate your time, sir. Thank you.

